lar at the time the movie set and  whose tracks appeared in the film's  trailers like 4town nsync's name also  includes an unspoken asterix the  all-white outfits worn by fortan during  their concert tour channel the cover of  the backstreet boys album millennium and  possibly take that's everything change's  album while the fictional boy band  angelic look could well have been  influenced by the backstreet boys role  in the apocalyptic comedy this is the  end which featured them in heaven all  dressed in white complete with halos  singing everybody there's a pop culture  reference to marvel comics and movies  where may cries first the symbol a twist  on avengers assemble and of course  marvel is owned by disney and there's a  nod to another franchise now owned by  disney the simpsons via the two red  panda statues who may lin refers to as  bart and lisa outside the ancestral  family temple hey bart  haley said when abby discovers red panda  may her reaction is hilarious you're so  fluffy which really reminds me of  despicable me's agnes and her obsession  with  unicorns it's just fluffy alternately it  could be a nod to this moment in disney  zootopia  hey you can't just touch a sheep's wall  the unicorn sticker on may's flute case  with its multi-coloured mane and tail  could be a little nod to rainbow unicorn  from inside out who joy sadness and bing  bong meet when they visit dream  productions  when ming turns into an enormous red  panda and stomps through the city on the  way to the concert i got some real  godzilla and king kong vibes especially  the scene of her roaring silhouette on a  toronto skyscraper and the way red panda  ming grabs melin in her giant paw is a  nod to the classic moment when king kong  grabs andaro up in his giant hand  there's also a ton of canada's specific  easter eggs and references in the movie  some are easier to spot like toronto cn  tower or this one 200  who do they think they are celine dion  but others are less obvious like 